{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Sci-fi panel close",
  "description": "The holographic panel folding away, the opposite of Sci-fi panel open in every way: everything falls, darkens and narrows, and the weight is before the snap. A low, hollow tone, lower than the open's chord, plays backwards, swelling up out of nothing, while air is drawn inward and down, a tonal glide powers down and glittering grains gather and fall inward; all of it is sucked into a heavy, dark latch with a firm sub thump. Then one quick power-off blip drops away, and it is over: a short, close room, no echo, no bloom.",
